#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "customer.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki To Customer Integration
	Testing Koroneiki To Customer Integration functionality.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate future static full start and end dates
	* I generate future static start and end dates
	* I generate static full start and end dates
	* I generate static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I generate future static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I generate static end dates
	* I generate static start dates
	* I generate future static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate static variables for a support user
	* I rename the first support user variables
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue1}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue1}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastNameValue1}  |
	* I generate static variables for a support user
	* I rename the second support user variables
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue2}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue2}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue2} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastNameValue2}  |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Cstpro - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                    |
	| Portal Production                 |
	| Commerce Subscription Development |
	| Platinum Subscription             |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                    |
	| Portal Production                 |
	| Commerce Subscription Development |
	| Platinum Subscription             |
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                    |
	| Portal Production                 |
	| Commerce Subscription Development |
	| Platinum Subscription             |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| CSTPROPROCST |
	| CSTPRO       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Procst - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Cstpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| CSTPROPROCST |
	| CSTPRO       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Procst - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Cstpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Procst - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Cstpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View DXP Production license on customer
    Testing the DXP Production license integration from koroneiki to customer

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Account Field and Value | liferayVersion                       | DXP 7.4 |
	| Code                    | CSTPROPROCST                         |         |
	| Contact Email Address   | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |         |
	| Description             | Test osb account on koroneiki        |         |
	| Fax Number              | 555-555-1234                         |         |
	| Name                    | Procst - ${staticProjectName}        |         |
	| Phone Number            | 555-555-5678                         |         |
	| Profile Email Address   | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |         |
	| Region                  | United States                        |         |
	| Status                  | Active                               |         |
	| Tier                    | T4                                   |         |
	| Website                 | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |         |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" on the account "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Administrator |
	And I log into the dev domain as "${staticEmailValue1}" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	And I generate the account key value for "Procst - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I generate the product purchase key value for the product purchase made by "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a license with the following parameters on the account "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" and product purchase "DXP Production" using okta session id with the following values
	| Name               | Procst - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name        |
	| Description        | Procst - ${staticProjectName} License1 Description |
	| Active             | true                                               |
	| Expiration Date    | ${staticEndDate}                                   |
	| License Entry Type | production                                         |
	| Max Cluster Nodes  | 0                                                  |
	| Product Version    | 7.4                                                |
	| Start Date         | ${staticStartDate}                                 |
	Then I should be able to view the license on the account "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Procst - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name" and the following filters
	| Name                  | Procst - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name        |
	| Complimentary         | false                                              |
	| Description           | Procst - ${staticProjectName} License1 Description |
	| Host Name             | localhost                                          |
	| IP Addresses          | 123.45.67.89                                       |
	| MAC Addresses         | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                                  |
	| Instance Size         | 1                                                  |
	| Maximum Cluster Nodes | 0                                                  |
	| Product Name          | DXP Production                                     |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be a member of the okta group "Customer"
	When I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Procst - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I click on the account with the name "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the Sync To Customer Portal button on the account page
	And I log out of the dev domain
	And I log into the customer homepage as "${staticEmailValue1}" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	And I click on the project with the name "Procst - ${staticProjectName}" on the customer project details page
	And I click on start project setup on setup pop up
	And I click on skip button on invite team members pop up
	And I choose the "DXP" subscription at the product activation tab
	And I search the activation key with the keyword "Procst - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then I should be able to view a Portal or DXP activation key with the environment name "Procst - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name" on product activation tab with the following values
	| Environment Name         | Procst - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name        |
	| Description              | Procst - ${staticProjectName} License1 Description |
	| Key Type                 | On-Premise                                         |
	| Host Name / Cluster Size | localhost                                          |
	| Environment Type         | DXP Production                                     |
#	| Expiration Date          | ${staticFullEndDate}                               |
	| Status                   | Activated                                          |

Scenario: View Portal Production license on customer
